window.TC_PORTRAITS=Object.assign(window.TC_PORTRAITS||{},{"pisces-aries-pisces":["Is it allowed, wanting something this much and this fast? You ask it half a second after the wanting arrives, which is the whole story of you. People meet a gentle voice and a gaze fixed somewhere past the argument. Then you stand up in the middle of an afternoon and leave the job, the conversation, the plan that was slowly closing around you. Your anger, when it comes, is brief, bright and over by evening. You are the only one still apologising for it at supper.","Your Aries Moon is the one light with an edge. The Pisces Sun and Pisces Rising speak the same soft language and share the same weakness: both let everything in, so neither is any good at a door. The Moon is the door. It sits one sign away, close enough to hear them and too different to be understood, so each side takes the other for an interruption. The Sun wants to serve what it senses. The Moon wants to move before the sensing is finished. Let the fire go first and the compassion second, in that order.","Courage that does not look like courage. You feel what a situation needs and are the first one on your feet, whether that means leaving, starting, or crossing a street to help a stranger. Your decisiveness arrives with such obvious kindness that people forgive the speed, and often thank you for it later.","You can swallow a small no for weeks until it goes off like a flare, then spend days soothing the damage and calling it your fault. Being cornered by other people’s needs is your real injury, and you may not see the corner until you are already shouting. Growth is saying the small no at the first flicker, while it is still a sentence and not yet an exit."],"pisces-taurus-pisces":["Picture three people in one house. The Sun sits at the upstairs window watching the sea for a sign, and would happily forget lunch. The Rising answers the door and says come in to everyone, so gently that strangers confide. The Moon is in the kitchen with its hands in the dough, and it has never agreed to be hurried. The world meets whoever is at the door. What keeps that person upright is a standing arrangement with soup, clean sheets and one chair that is always the same chair.","Your Taurus Moon is exalted, an honoured guest in the house, and it sits a sextile from your Pisces lights, so these three can cooperate whenever you ask them to. The task is to ask. Left alone, the two Pisces lights drift together and agree about everything, including a weekend your body cannot afford. The Moon is the voice that says you are tired. It is fixed, unhurried and unmoved by cosmic reasons. Honour it and the Sun’s visions get a kitchen to be cooked in. Ignore it and it sulks, over something absurdly small like a particular mug.","You make idealism edible. Your visions arrive with bread, a made bed and follow-through, so the people you love feel understood and fed in the same hour. Your calm is physical: a hand on the shoulder, a pot left warm on the stove, a place for the exhausted to land and be quiet.","Comfort can become the harbour you never leave. The Pisces habit of soaking up other people’s moods finds a Taurus remedy: another evening in, another favourite programme, the same four streets. You are slow to anger and slower to forgive, so a grievance may sit in the pantry for years, labelled as nothing. Growth is letting the Sun’s faraway call move you a little, then coming home to the table."],"pisces-gemini-pisces":["By fifty you understand what you can only circle at twenty: explaining a feeling is not the same as having it, and you did both so fast that nobody, yourself included, could tell them apart. People meet a listening presence, unhurried and half in a daydream. Then you open your mouth and out comes something funny, well read and surprisingly nimble. The contrast is part of your charm. You keep a running commentary on your own life, and talking it through is how you find out what you think.","Your Gemini Moon squares the Pisces pair, and since all three lights are mutable, none of them has the habit of holding a line. The friction is between naming and dissolving. The Moon needs a feeling put into a sentence before it can rest. The Sun and Rising know that the best part of any feeling is the part sentences miss. So you talk, and it is never quite right, and so you talk again. The useful trick, learned over years, is to let one friend hear the unfinished version and let silence do the editing.","Translation. You can carry a feeling into language and carry someone’s confusion back out of it, which makes you a wonderful letter-writer, teacher, interpreter or friend on the phone at midnight. You ask the question that lets people discover what they meant, and you do it without making them feel studied.","Talking can become a way of staying one step ahead of the feeling. You describe the sadness charmingly, to three different people, and are surprised that it has not moved. With every light mutable, you may also agree with whoever spoke last. Growth is staying with one unnamed feeling for the length of a song, and letting the words arrive after it instead of in its place."],"pisces-cancer-pisces":["At the door you press a container of soup into a friend’s hands, tell them to bring the dish back whenever, and stand on the step until their car turns the corner. That is the whole of you in one gesture. You remember every birthday, every hospital appointment, the name of every dog. Strangers meet something gentle and hazy. Friends learn that nothing said to you in confidence has ever gone further. Your feelings are weather that never quite clears, and your home is where it is finally allowed to break.","All three lights are water, and your Cancer Moon trines the Pisces pair, so nothing in the chart pushes against anything else. That is a gift and a cost. Feeling moves between the three of you without friction, which means no light ever says stop. The Sun wants to merge with the world’s sorrow, the Rising lets it in at the door, and the Moon, at home in its own sign, offers it a bed. Nobody outside the system asks whether the guest has stayed too long. Your discipline is not to feel less. It is to build one wall with a door in it.","Holding. You make a room feel as though someone has been expecting everyone in it. You can sit with grief without hurrying it, remember what mattered to a person years later, and make loss feel witnessed. People arrive tired and leave with the sense that being tired was acceptable.","Water with no shoreline floods. You can take on a family’s mood, a friend’s heartbreak, a stranger’s headline, and be unable to tell which ache is yours. Care becomes a way of never being alone, and you may hold on past the point where holding helps. Growth is letting someone else carry the cup for an hour, and learning that being needed is not the same as being safe."],"pisces-leo-pisces":["You disappear into every room and ache to be noticed in it. The contradiction is simple once you see it. What you show is receptive and half turned toward the horizon, so people project their own pictures onto you and applaud those. Your Leo Moon watches the applause and goes hungry, because none of it was for you. What you want is to be seen: the silly song, the extravagant gesture, the colour you secretly love. With two or three trusted people you become the warmest, funniest host in the building.","Leo and Pisces sit five signs apart, a quincunx, with no element or modality in common, so Moon and Sun behave like relatives who have never been introduced. The Pisces lights hand their warmth to everyone. The Leo Moon wants some of it returned, in colour, by name. Because Sun and Rising speak one language, the Moon is the only light that knows how to ask for anything, and it asks sideways: a costume, a theatrical sigh, a present slightly too large. Your task is to seat the Sun’s humility and the Moon’s pride at one table.","Generosity with style. You make other people feel like the best version of themselves, then do it again with a joke and a flourish. You can run a children’s table, a grieving room or a stage with the same open-handed warmth, and your creative work carries the unmistakable sense of being made for someone.","The wound is being overlooked, and the habit is to hide it. You give the biggest gift, wait to see whether anyone notices its size, and quietly keep score of the silence. Pride and self-erasure take turns running the household. Growth is asking, in plain words, for what you need, and trusting that you are allowed to be someone’s favourite part of the day."],"pisces-virgo-pisces":["People read you as vague: the one who lets the plan wander, speaks softly and looks out of the window. The truth is nearly the reverse. You know where the spare key is, which bill falls due on Thursday, and what the quiet guest in the corner did not eat. Worry is your private weather, and a cleared counter is the closest thing you have to a prayer. Where others see a floating mystic, you are the unpaid quartermaster of every room you walk into.","Virgo stands opposite Pisces, and your Moon is the only light on that side, so the chart is a seesaw: two lights on one end, one on the other, all three mutable. The Sun and Rising pour out and merge. The Moon sorts, repairs and counts. Each is the other’s missing half, which is why you may project them onto people, the chaotic friend who needs fixing, the practical partner who seems cold. The Sun asks for faith. The Moon asks for a list. When they quarrel, the Sun floats, the Moon audits, and you feel both as guilt.","Devotion with a method. You turn compassion into something deliverable: the meal arrives, the form is filled in, the appointment is remembered, and nobody has to ask. You notice small physical needs that more visionary people miss, and your quiet competence makes hard weeks survivable for everyone around you.","You can be so useful that nobody learns you have needs. Anxiety goes unspoken and surfaces as fixing: re-sorting a drawer, re-reading an email, finding the fault in something you could simply enjoy. Your self-criticism has none of the Sun’s gentleness. Growth is letting one task stay undone for an evening and finding that the house, and your worth, are still there in the morning."],"pisces-libra-pisces":["Your shoulders lift an inch before you know why. In the next room someone is annoyed with someone, and your body has filed the report before your mind opens it. You stand with your weight on one foot, head slightly tilted, ready to turn toward whoever speaks. People meet a gentle, absorbed listener. What they miss is how much of your day goes on keeping the atmosphere breathable: moving the conversation along, softening the sentence, noticing who was left out of it. You need a companion the way other people need sleep.","Libra and Pisces are five signs apart and share neither element nor modality, so your Moon and Sun keep re-introducing themselves. Libra reaches for fairness and a witness. Pisces reaches for union and the unseen. The Moon wants the two of you to agree, while the Sun and Rising want to dissolve into the other person so completely that the question of agreement disappears. You end up keeping the peace by vanishing, which looks like harmony and feels like a held breath. The Moon’s gift to the pair is language: it can turn a mood into a sentence and a quarrel into terms.","Reconciliation. You can sit between two people who have run out of words and find the sentence both can bear. You bring grace and a sense of fairness into rooms that have lost both, and your sympathy arrives with good manners, which makes it easy to accept.","Peace can become the price you pay for being liked. You say yes to the restaurant, the plan, the version of events, and discover three days later that your own preference never entered the conversation. Resentment collects in the body, in the clenched jaw and the lifted shoulders. Growth is letting a room be uncomfortable for ten minutes while you say what you want."],"pisces-scorpio-pisces":["At three in the morning you are awake with a sentence someone said in March. By day you are the forgiver, the one who says it is fine and means it with the part of you that can. The Scorpio part keeps a different record. It does not shout and it does not forget. Betrayal does not fade for you; it hardens, then goes quiet, which is how people find they have been left without ever hearing why. Almost no one meets this side. Those who are let in find a loyalty with no floor.","Three water lights and a trine mean the current runs one way without a snag. The Scorpio Moon is in its fall, which is why its power arrives through humility and not force: it is learned by being wrong in front of someone and surviving it. The Sun forgives, the Rising soothes, and the Moon archives, so your gentle self signs treaties your private self has not ratified. The ease between them is the trap. Nothing outside ever contradicts the story, so a hurt can set into certainty with nobody to check it.","Depth you can trust. You are very hard to fool and very hard to shock, and you can sit through someone’s worst confession without flinching or repeating it. Your loyalty is total once given, and people sense that they can put the unspeakable thing down in your keeping and find it there later.","The silence is the danger. A hurt left unspoken at the soft stage becomes a closed door at the hard one, and others are left guessing what they did. You may grieve a friendship that you ended without telling anyone. Growth is saying the hurt aloud while it is still water, before it sets, and letting forgiveness be a decision made with the memory intact."],"pisces-sagittarius-pisces":["A flock of shorebirds lifts off the mudflat all at once, turns toward open sea and trusts a coast none of them has seen. That is your Moon, and it is allowed to decide your week. You are warm, laughing and philosophical, always about to begin something, with a pile of unread travel books and a half-packed bag under the bed. People meet the drifting, receptive Pisces and are startled by how much horizon you carry in your pockets. Your faith is contagious because you have not been talked out of it.","Sagittarius and Pisces share Jupiter in the old scheme, so Moon, Sun and Rising answer to one patron, and that gives all three a trust that things will be provided for. They square each other, though, and the friction is real. The Moon wants a horizon. The Sun and Rising want to dissolve into whoever is standing in front of them. You vow to leave, then stay to comfort someone. With every light mutable you adapt beautifully and decide badly. The Moon is your best defence against being absorbed by other people’s problems.","Faith that can be borrowed. You carry hope into rooms where it has run out and convince tired people that the road continues. You are generous with attention, at ease with large questions, and a natural bridge between cultures, beliefs and the grief of someone who needed a window opened.","Optimism can be a door left ajar so you never have to stay for the hard part. You promise generously, then slip out in the name of freedom or higher meaning, and others pay the cost. Faith without follow-through becomes a lovely fog. Growth is staying through the dull middle of one thing long enough to learn what it has to teach."],"pisces-capricorn-pisces":["When you are tired, upset or secretly delighted, you make a list. The gentle face you show the world has nothing to do with it; that face simply lets everyone in. Behind it a sober, private part of you handles feelings as a job to be done properly, on time and without fuss. You pay the bill before telling anyone the week was hard. People expect a drifter and are surprised by how reliably you turn up. Your tenderness travels as provision: the lift to the station, the quietly settled debt, the spare key.","Capricorn is the Moon’s detriment, so it works against the grain, and the sextile to your Pisces lights says it can still cooperate if you use it. The use is this. The Sun supplies vision and the Rising supplies access to other people’s pain, and the Moon gives both a structure to be carried in. Unstructured, Pisces floods. Unfed, Capricorn goes cold. Your Moon was not built to ask for comfort, so that skill has to be learned as deliberately as any other. The pier is the picture: something solid reaching out over water without trying to be the water.","Compassion with a spine. You turn the sense of what is needed into schedules, funds, shelters and systems that outlast your mood. You are calm in other people’s crises and can be counted on at the worst hour, and your steadiness is more convincing because it comes from someone visibly gentle.","You may mistake being useful for being close, and keep the feeling in a locked drawer marked later. The Pisces face invites everyone’s trouble, and the Capricorn Moon takes it on as duty and tells no one the price. Weariness arrives as a cold, flat efficiency. Growth is letting a person see the unfinished sentence, and accepting help before the list runs out."],"pisces-aquarius-pisces":["Why do I love people best from slightly further away? You ask it in the car park after a party, keys in hand, warm from three hours of being everyone’s confidant and desperate for silence. What you show invites people closer, and you let them, while the Moon quietly counts the minutes. You are loyal, odd, friendly with half the street and intimate with very few. You feel enormous things in a cool register, and you tend to describe them as if they happened in an interesting country.","Aquarius sits next to Pisces on the wheel, the semi-sextile: neighbours who share neither element nor modality, each barely able to see the other. The Sun and Rising dissolve into the person in front of you. The Moon, fixed and airy, wants a window and a friend who will not need you to merge. So your closeness has two speeds, flood and withdrawal, and the people near you only ever see the withdrawal. The fixed Moon is also the one stubborn thing in a chart of drifters. What it protects is your right to be strange.","Compassion without clinging. You can care about people, causes and strangers at a scale that would flatten a more fusional person, because you give from a little distance as well as from warmth. You are the friend who accepts the odd, the unconventional and the unfinished, and your ideas have heart in them.","Distance can pass for peace. You may tell yourself you are fine because the feeling has been turned into an idea, an observation or a plan to improve the world, while the person beside you waits for an answer that has no abstract in it. Growth is letting one person be close enough to see you uncertain, and finding that closeness and freedom are not opposites."],"pisces-pisces-pisces":["Three of you live in this house, all made of water, and they still want different things. The Sun wants to be of use to something larger than itself. The Rising wants to be kind to whoever knocks. The Moon wants the door locked, a bath running and a record on. The world meets the second: soft-voiced, so receptive that people tell you things they have not told themselves. Alone, the third takes over and spends an hour discovering that half of what it feels belonged to someone else.","A triple conjunction is total coherence and no outside view. Sun, Moon and Rising speak one dialect, so nothing in the chart interrupts, corrects or says that is enough. That is how you can sense the exact mood of a room and still be unsure what you personally want. The three lights do have different jobs: purpose, need, entrance. But they pour into the same pool and cannot tell each other apart without help. What you need is something fixed from outside: a schedule, a friend who says what is yours and what is theirs, a shoreline built on purpose.","Attunement. You perceive what people cannot say and give it back to them as music, as a hand on the arm, as silence made safe. In art, caregiving and any craft that needs listening, you work from a depth others spend years approaching, and you can make a stranger feel less alone with one sentence.","Without edges the feeling comes in unfiltered: other people’s moods, the news, the atmosphere of a bad week, all in your body as if they were yours. You may escape into sleep or scrolling, then wonder why you are so tired. Growth is learning boundaries slowly, as a craft: one clear no, one scheduled hour of solitude, one habit that tells you where you end."]});
